Z||000000||Richard Parnell||06-15-2001||02:41 PM||||I want to replace all the bushings on the front suspension of my '87 coupe and as much as can be replaced in the rear without removing the cradle.  I read about cwests' delrin bushings.  I like the fact that the entire set is already sold as a package.  When I look at other sites I get confused as to what parts I need to order because all the parts are listed seperately.  Or should I just get everything including the upper and lowwer ball joints?  Also does cwest have tie rod ends?  I didn't see them listed.  I was told on my last inspection that they were worn. My car is beginning to not handle well steering wise and I would like to tighten everything up so I can run it through the 1/4 mile to see what she'll do.  Right now I'm afraid to go too fast the way it sits.  Also one last question I'm going to replace the front shocks and rear struts with monroe, Should I change out the rear springs for some heftier ones.  I don't want the car to sit any higher though. I know lots of questions in this topic but any help would be appreciated.  ||||reg||5
